<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paynes Prairie</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Alachua Savanna, Alachua prairie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paynes Prairie is a large savanna and wetland basin south of Gainesville in north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, known in the 18th century as the Alachua prairie. Around 1750 the chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cowkeeper">Cowkeeper</a> led settlers there, and his town of Cuscowilla became a centre of the emerging Seminole people. The prairie takes its name from his successor Payne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paynes-prairie.jpg" alt="Paynes Prairie" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Operator 16 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paynes_Prairie_Preserve_State_Park_25.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
